#X text 240 83 Runs the given external command in a separate process
and outputs its exit code and stdout as a list of strings. The process
can be controlled via the eof \, stop and terminate methods \, and
additional data can be sent to its stdin with the write method.;
#X text 240 168 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 193 • Running scripts and tools from a patch — executing
external programs (Python scripts \, ffmpeg \, custom utilities) directly
from Pd and using their output to drive the patch or trigger further
actions.;
